{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `Yvec1`, `y0`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: reordered the model block so all parameter priors occur before the parameters are used. Replaced the indexed loop likelihood for `y0[n]` with the equivalent vectorized statement `y0 ~ normal(mu0, sigma_y)`, so the protected data variable is observed exactly once with a plain top-level identifier. Removed the `transformed data` use of protected `y0` and recomputed `y0_mean` in the model block after `y0` has been observed. The supplied data are unchanged; no fields were added.
","model_safe_stan":"// Hepatitis: a normal hierarchical model with measurement 
// error
//  http://openbugs.net/Examples/Hepatitis.html

// model the measurement eror here (compared with hepatitis.stan) 

//# note that we have missing data in the orignal data Y[N, T]; 
//# here, we turn Y[N, T] into Yvec with the missing
//# data removed.  

data {
  int<lower=0> N1; //# N1 is the length of the vector, Yvec1, that is 
  int<lower=0> N; //# created from concatenate columns of matrix Y[N, T] 
  array[N1] real Yvec1; //# with NA's removed. 
  array[N1] real tvec1; //# N is the nrow of original matrix Y[N, T] 
  array[N1] int<lower=0> idxn1; //# idxn1 maps Yvec to its orignal n index 
  array[N] real y0;
}
parameters {
  real<lower=0> sigmasq_y;
  real<lower=0> sigmasq_alpha;
  real<lower=0> sigmasq_beta;
  real<lower=0> sigma_mu0;
  real gamma;
  real alpha0;
  real beta0;
  real theta;
  array[N] real mu0;
  array[N] real alpha;
  array[N] real beta;
}
transformed parameters {
  real<lower=0> sigma_y;
  real<lower=0> sigma_alpha;
  real<lower=0> sigma_beta;
  sigma_y = sqrt(sigmasq_y);
  sigma_alpha = sqrt(sigmasq_alpha);
  sigma_beta = sqrt(sigmasq_beta);
}
model {
  int oldn;
  real y0_mean;
  array[N1] real m;

  sigmasq_y ~ inv_gamma(.001, .001);
  sigmasq_alpha ~ inv_gamma(.001, .001);
  sigmasq_beta ~ inv_gamma(.001, .001);
  sigma_mu0 ~ inv_gamma(.001, .001);

  alpha0 ~ normal(0, 1000);
  beta0 ~ normal(0, 1000);
  gamma ~ normal(0, 1000);
  theta ~ normal(0, 1000);

  mu0 ~ normal(theta, sigma_mu0);
  alpha ~ normal(alpha0, sigma_alpha);
  beta ~ normal(beta0, sigma_beta);

  y0 ~ normal(mu0, sigma_y);

  y0_mean = mean(y0);
  for (n in 1 : N1) {
    oldn = idxn1[n];
    m[n] = alpha[oldn] + beta[oldn] * (tvec1[n] - 6.5)
           + gamma * (mu0[oldn] - y0_mean);
  }
  Yvec1 ~ normal(m, sigma_y);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N":3,"N1":1,"Yvec1":[3.4824489387368085],"idxn1":[2],"tvec1":[5.032034979736335],"y0":[6.311556680633488,4.937447094434329,6.029871123716202]}","protected_variables":["Yvec1","y0"]}
